# Findings this project has looked at and accepted. Anything not listed here
# is reported by `make scan-code` and by CI.
#
# Nothing in this file suppresses a vulnerability. It is misconfiguration
# rules only, and each one needs a reason.

# DS-0002: "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user"
#
# A must-gather image cannot run as a non-root user. It reads /host on the
# node through a privileged debug pod, runs `oc adm node-logs` against the
# kubelet, and writes into a directory the copy sidecar owns. Upstream's own
# Dockerfile has no USER line either, and adding one would stop the image
# collecting anything.
#
# Also fires on vendor/github.com/openshift/build-machinery-go/
# Dockerfile.commitchecker, which is vendored upstream tooling and not built
# by this repo at all.
DS-0002
